From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreELEC <team@coreelec.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: add quirks for HyperX Cloud II USB dongle

The HyperX Cloud II USB dongle (0951:16a4, "Kingston HyperX 7.1 Audio")
requires the same 1ms delay after USB class requests as the Cloud
Revolver S (0951:16ad). Without it, get/set frequency requests fail
intermittently during enumeration on kernel 4.9, causing unreliable
device recognition, audio latency spikes, and channel mapping failures
that manifest as mono output or reverb-like artifacts.

Also add the device to snd_usb_get_sample_rate_quirk() to skip the
UAC GET_CUR sample rate readback, as the dongle firmware does not
reliably respond to it on this kernel, causing repeated error retries
that contribute to the observed audio delay on first playback.

Note: mainline kernel fixed Cloud II detection in 4.10 via a different
path; this backport applies the same class of fix suitable for 4.9.

Signed-off-by: CoreELEC <team@coreelec.org>
---
diff --git a/sound/usb/quirks.c b/sound/usb/quirks.c
index 02b4d0638e00..22d47facc24f 100644
--- a/sound/usb/quirks.c
+++ b/sound/usb/quirks.c
@@ -1141,6 +1141,7 @@ bool snd_usb_get_sample_rate_quirk(struct snd_usb_audio *chip)
 	switch (chip->usb_id) {
 	case USB_ID(0x041E, 0x4080): /* Creative Live Cam VF0610 */
 	case USB_ID(0x045E, 0x075D): /* MS Lifecam Cinema  */
+	case USB_ID(0x0951, 0x16a4): /* Kingston HyperX Cloud II dongle */
 	case USB_ID(0x045E, 0x076D): /* MS Lifecam HD-5000 */
 	case USB_ID(0x045E, 0x076E): /* MS Lifecam HD-5001 */
 	case USB_ID(0x045E, 0x076F): /* MS Lifecam HD-6000 */
@@ -1333,11 +1334,13 @@ void snd_usb_ctl_msg_quirk(struct usb_device *dev, unsigned int pipe,
 	/* Zoom R16/24, Logitech H650e/H570e, Jabra 550a, Kingston HyperX
 	 *  needs a tiny delay here, otherwise requests like get/set
 	 *  frequency return as failed despite actually succeeding.
+	 * HyperX Cloud II dongle (16a4) has the same timing requirement.
 	 */
 	if ((chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x1686, 0x00dd) ||
 	     chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x046d, 0x0a46) ||
 	     chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x046d, 0x0a56) ||
 	     chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0b0e, 0x0349) ||
+	     chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0951, 0x16a4) ||
 	     chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0951, 0x16ad)) &&
 	    (requesttype & USB_TYPE_MASK) == USB_TYPE_CLASS)
 		mdelay(1);
-- 
